Promote the IPsec tunnel a REGISTER came in over.

ims_ipsec_pcscf keeps a contact's offered tunnel beside the one the UE is
registered over until the UE has registered over the offer (TS 33.203 7.4),
and leaves the handover to ipsec_promote(). update_contacts() calls it for each
contact a 200 to a REGISTER updates, with the REGISTER's receive info: only one
that came in over the offer promotes it, so a refresh that was not challenged,
or another contact's REGISTER, changes nothing.

checkcontact() accepts the protected client port of either tunnel: until the
200, the UE still sends over the one it is registered over.

diff --git a/src/modules/ims_registrar_pcscf/save.c b/src/modules/ims_registrar_pcscf/save.c
index 6e697c03b9..98acf96464 100644
--- a/src/modules/ims_registrar_pcscf/save.c
+++ b/src/modules/ims_registrar_pcscf/save.c
@@ -321,6 +321,14 @@ static inline int update_contacts(struct sip_msg *req, struct sip_msg *rpl,
 								LM_DBG("Error subscribing for contact\n");
 							}
 
+							// A REGISTER answered over the tunnel the last 401
+							// offered makes it the one the UE is registered
+							// over, and retires the one it replaces
+							if(ipsec_pcscf.ipsec_promote != NULL) {
+								ipsec_pcscf.ipsec_promote(
+										_d, pcontact, &req->rcv);
+							}
+
 							// After successful registration try to unregister all callbacks for pending contacts related to this contact.
 							ul.unreg_pending_contacts_cb(
 									_d, pcontact, PCSCF_CONTACT_EXPIRE);
